{
  "id": "auditory-object",
  "term": "auditory object",
  "definition": "An auditory object is a perceived sound pattern, such as speech or music, that listeners recognize as the same and meaningful even when its exact acoustic form changes. Its perceived identity is shaped not only by the sound itself but also by prior experience, immediate context, and the listener’s goals and expectations.",
